  "sourceBoundContracts": [
    "SwDoc GetRowSplit compares GetValue on collected original lines and returns an independent concrete item; SetRowSplit accepts const native item and records original selected row attributes including same-value operations.",
    "Row format input/read/history owns cloned native SwFormatRowSplit; effective default true, core and frame shell APIs retain the item, mounted main UI forwards native items through the original document graph without scalar stripping.",
    "XML imports original table-row attributes into the row frame format; native row export checks explicit RES_ROW_SPLIT. xmloff IsSplitAllowed maps inverse keep-together at the XML boundary. Primitive browser rowSplit retains optional authoring, legacy inverse ingress only.",
    "Native border page has exchange support; tabdlg Ok excludes exchange pages from FillItemSet, and native tabsh temporary selection admits only explicit borders or row items. Exactly three stale old unvisited-Borders call expectations migrate to zero; every other old assertion, including legacy DTO history, retained."
  ],
  "residuals": [
    "Full native shared SwTableLineFormat ownership/GetFrameFormat/ClaimFrameFormat/pooling/refcounts and merged/nested/row-span behavior remain unverified.",
    "Full localization/presentation/UNO, table scalar format ownership and browser/native widget orchestration remain partial. Legacy explicit DTO compatibility remains separate from main mounted native UI and is not claimed as native dialog parity.",
    "Registered IO/recovery/settings and all prior metadata states/defaults/classes preserved; whole core/browser parity incomplete."
  ]
}
